{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Or flesh torn in the field, etc.</b> Since the dog risked its life for the torn animal when the wolf came to prey upon it, do not be ungrateful toward it — so when you have a torn animal, throw it to him as reward for having guarded it until now so it was not preyed upon, and for still guarding the others as well, for thus is the way of the world to station dogs to guard the flocks from wolves."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:55.257258584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}